1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,443
Because mixtures aren't chemically joined, we can separate them physically.

2
00:00:04,443 --> 00:00:07,834
Handpicking removes large pieces by hand or with forceps.

3
00:00:07,834 --> 00:00:12,453
Sieving separates large particles from small ones: the small ones fall through.

4
00:00:13,512 --> 00:00:16,727
Filtration separates an insoluble solid from a liquid.

5
00:00:16,727 --> 00:00:20,995
The liquid passes through filter paper and is collected as the filtrate,

6
00:00:20,995 --> 00:00:23,568
while the solid stays behind as the residue.

7
00:00:24,626 --> 00:00:28,017
Evaporation separates a dissolved solute from a solution.

8
00:00:28,017 --> 00:00:33,279
Heat it, the solvent evaporates, and the solute is left behind, like salt from salt water.

9
00:00:34,337 --> 00:00:36,384
Distillation collects the solvent.

10
00:00:36,384 --> 00:00:41,353
The mixture is heated; the substance with the lowest boiling point evaporates first,

11
00:00:41,353 --> 00:00:47,726
then cools and condenses back into a liquid, called the distillate. This can turn salt water into pure water.

12
00:00:48,784 --> 00:00:53,988
A dot of black felt-tip ink is put on a pencil line near the bottom of a strip of paper.

13
00:00:53,988 --> 00:01:00,477
The bottom edge stands in water. Predict: will the ink stay as one black spot as the water soaks up the paper?

14
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:01,471
Pause and decide.

15
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:06,154
Watch. The water soaks slowly up the paper, past the ink spot.

16
00:01:07,213 --> 00:01:13,703
The black ink separates into three coloured spots at different heights: yellow at the top, then red, then blue.

17
00:01:14,761 --> 00:01:17,918
Explain what you saw. Black ink is a mixture of dyes.

18
00:01:17,918 --> 00:01:23,882
Each dye dissolves in the water, but travels up the paper at a different speed, so the dyes separate.

19
00:01:23,882 --> 00:01:30,371
The yellow dye moved furthest. This method is paper chromatography. A pure substance would give only one spot.

20
00:01:30,371 --> 00:01:32,651
Pause and explain it in your own words.

21
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:39,147
Chromatography separates substances that dissolve in the same solvent, like the dyes in ink.

22
00:01:39,147 --> 00:01:43,298
Draw a pencil line near the bottom of special paper, add a dot of ink,

23
00:01:43,298 --> 00:01:48,560
and dip the end in a solvent such as water or alcohol, keeping the line above the solvent.

24
00:01:49,618 --> 00:01:53,360
As the solvent soaks up the paper, it carries the dyes with it.

25
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:59,499
Each dye travels at a different speed, so they separate into spots. The result is called a chromatogram.

26
00:01:59,499 --> 00:02:02,832
This brown ink contains three dyes: blue, red and yellow.

27
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:07,223
A pure substance gives just one spot, like this red ink.

28
00:02:07,223 --> 00:02:12,251
Chromatography is used to check the nutritional value of food, measure blood glucose,

29
00:02:12,251 --> 00:02:13,946
and test water for pollution.
